CREATED-BY: 5MContest ver. 8.0.14
SOAPBOX: As in SSB part it was hard to work in East direction due to high local noise.
SOAPBOX: Although I checked band on friday morning before the contest and there was no extra noise.
SOAPBOX: But the neighbors come at their home on the weekend and apparently some house equipment were turned on.
SOAPBOX: Also I'd like to point out few long time phenomenons of HF contesting:
SOAPBOX: 1) It seems like most wants to just call CQs, and do it too much, hi.
SOAPBOX: But if almost of all like to do CQ, then note that less people will
SOAPBOX: do S&P and respond to that CQ.
SOAPBOX: General ask to serious participants - do more S&P work, its easy now
SOAPBOX: with spots and contest software, radios with second receiver/vfo etc!
SOAPBOX: Its a good way to improve operating skills.
SOAPBOX: 2) On the other hand, I've noticed that many modest stations participants
SOAPBOX: don't trying to do CQ at all! So its quite lucky (for CQ station) if they
SOAPBOX: respond to it.
SOAPBOX: However in about a decade, an automatic skimmers have been operating worldwide
SOAPBOX: in CW and RTTY modes, and even with a weak signal, someone will always see
SOAPBOX: where you are and come to your CQ-calls!
SOAPBOX: Therefore, I encourage low-power stations to do some CQ calls as well.
SOAPBOX: This increases the chance of contacting you to every else!
SOAPBOX: (not only for a lucky CQ'ers that you are gives a calls to them).
